      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly state that “autonomous” means “rather than being directly driven by the user,” so that substantive definitional contrast is not supported.",
        "The definition says “built-in motion control affects how safe, reliable, and usable it feels”; the packet supports that motion control parameters (e.g., deceleration profiles and speed) affect usability ratings (including safety) and trust-related perceptions (including reliability/safety), but it does not clearly establish the phrase “built-in motion control” as part of the definition of “autonomous” itself."
